{
  "_comment": "What planets can be. A planet is one biome, atmosphere, terrain, weather and civilization, plus any specials, each picked by weight among the ones that suit it: a biome only where the planet's warmth (degrees C) falls in its 'temperature', and the others from the biome's own lists. Add an entry to add a kind of world. Names are what a player is shown; ids are what saves use, so do not rename an id once campaigns exist. Colours are 0-1 RGB.",

  "names": {
    "_comment": "Systems are a star catalogue and a number ('GLIESE-2174'), one of several catalogues so they are not all alike, planets after them by numeral ('GLIESE-2174 IV'). Moons have designations of their own, a prefix and a number ('LV-426'), as moons do in the Alien films.",
